<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24908" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">irrădĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inr-</span></b> ), āre,
			v. a. and n.
		1. inradio, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to illumine</i>, <i>irradiate; to beam
				forth</i>, <i>cast forth rays</i> (<b>poet.</b> and post-class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hoc undique gemmae irradiant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 6, 64</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">artes Romanis floribus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. Cons. Mall. Theod. 84</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Neutr.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">coeperat felix Irradiare dies,</span>”
				<i>to dawn</i>, <i>break</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sedul. 5, 315</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ambros. Apol. Dav. 8, §
			45</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
